    title: "微軟與AXA XL合作，強化網路事件響應：提供整合技術、法律與保險決策支援",
    summary: "本文介紹微軟（Microsoft）與全球保險公司AXA XL的合作，旨在建立一套更全面的網路事件響應模型。在當今AI加速的網路攻擊時代，事件響應已超越單純的技術修復，必須涵蓋技術、業務、法律和保險等多個面向的平行協調。透過此合作，AXA XL的保單持有者可直接獲得微軟Defender Experts的資安事件響應服務。這套整合模型結合了微軟的威脅情報、兩十年的實戰經驗，以及保險、法律和監管流程，確保在發生勒索軟體或重大入侵時，各方決策能同步進行，從而減少摩擦、延遲和不確定性。微軟的服務不僅限於危機發生時，也提供事前規劃、模擬演練和諮詢服務，幫助組織建立預防和應對的韌性，確保在危機來臨時能執行協調的計畫。",
    tags: ["Microsoft", "AXA XL", "資安事件響應", "網路韌性", "保險科技", "Defender Experts"],
    title_en: "Microsoft and AXA XL Partner to Enhance Cyber Incident Response: Providing Integrated Technology, Legal, and Insurance Decision Support",
    summary_en: "This article introduces the collaboration between Microsoft and the global insurance company AXA XL, aiming to establish a more comprehensive cyber incident response model. In today's era of AI-accelerated cyber attacks, incident response has moved beyond mere technical remediation, requiring parallel coordination across technology, business, legal, and insurance dimensions. Through this partnership, AXA XL policyholders can directly access Microsoft Defender Experts' cybersecurity incident response services. This integrated model combines Microsoft's threat intelligence, two decades of practical experience, and insurance, legal, and regulatory processes, ensuring that decision-making by all parties proceeds synchronously during ransomware attacks or major intrusions. This minimizes friction, delay, and uncertainty. Microsoft's services are not limited to crisis situations; they also provide proactive planning, simulation exercises, and consulting services, helping organizations build resilience for prevention and response, ensuring coordinated plans can be executed when a crisis strikes.",
    tags_en: ["Microsoft", "AXA XL", "Cyber Incident Response", "Cyber Resilience", "Insurtech", "Defender Experts"],
    sources: [
      { name: "Microsoft Security Blog", url: "https://microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2026/07/22/real-world-incident-response-microsoft-and-axa-xl-strengthen-cyber-resilience", lang: "EN" }
    ]
