    summary_en: "Swiss multinational rail manufacturer Stadler Rail encountered a cyberattack in mid-July, targeting a data exchange platform shared with its suppliers. The attackers, affiliated with the Everest ransomware group, demanded a ransom of approximately $12.3 million. Stadler Rail firmly stated that it would not pay any ransom and has reported the incident to local police. According to the company's disclosure, the hackers only stole technical information from the supplier and did not steal any personal data related to security. Stadler emphasized that its global rail vehicle and production operations were unaffected and continued to operate normally. The Everest group has shifted from network encryption to data theft threats, previously acting as a broker selling compromised network access. This incident serves as a reminder to enterprises that even if personal privacy data is not involved, supply chain data exchange platforms remain potential attack vectors, necessitating enhanced supply chain security and monitoring.",
