    summary_en: "The Linux kernel development team recently released a security update containing 432 CVEs in a single batch. This batch of updates covers multiple core components, indicating that the Linux kernel ecosystem continues to face widespread and complex vulnerability risks. The discovery and patching of these vulnerabilities have extremely high practical implications for system administrators using specific Linux distributions or relying on core components. All system administrators are advised to closely monitor the official security announcements of their used Linux distributions (such as Ubuntu, Debian, RHEL, etc.) and perform timely kernel-level upgrades and patches to ensure system security. Due to the sheer volume of vulnerabilities, it is recommended that upgrades be conducted in a phased and tested manner to avoid introducing new system instabilities.",
