    title_en: "iOS 27: Apple Wallet adds 'Recurring' feature, allowing users to track all subscription services at a glance",
    summary_en: "In iOS 27, Apple updated the Apple Wallet application for Apple Card users by adding a 'Recurring' feature. This feature allows users, when viewing their Apple Card account, to access the expected recurring deduction list via the three-dot menu in the upper right corner. It even provides a calendar view, enabling users to easily grasp the deduction time and amount for all subscription services. This feature directly integrates with the user's transaction history, greatly simplifying the process of tracking subscriptions and avoiding the privacy risk of providing personal financial information to third-party applications. The article notes that the predicted dates and amounts are based solely on transaction history and may not be completely accurate; if there are discrepancies, users can manually correct them. This update is considered a practical feature that all credit cards should possess.",
