    summary_en: "Apple has released the second public beta of macOS 27 Golden Gate, allowing users to participate in testing via beta.apple.com. The focus of this update is integrating a more powerful Siri AI experience, enabling it to index content from applications like Messages and Mail to answer questions and execute requests. Furthermore, macOS 27 Golden Gate significantly improves the Spotlight search function, fixing instability issues present in the previous version (macOS Tahoe 26). On the interface front, the system adjusts the Liquid Glass effect and adopts a unified corner radius for windows and applications. Additionally, Apple Intelligence features have been enhanced, including more efficient writing tools and a new Safari extension builder. Developers have also added a shortcut creation feature that can be generated from natural language commands. As this is a beta version, users may encounter various bugs, ranging from minor inconveniences to device malfunctions, and are advised to monitor system stability.",
