    summary_en: "According to an in-depth report by Bloomberg, Apple's product update plan for its Mac lineup over the next few years is taking shape. In the short term, Apple is expected to launch entry-level MacBook Pro models with M6 chips, new iMacs, and high-end 14-inch and 16-inch MacBook series equipped with OLED screens. These high-end models are anticipated to be released between the end of this year and early next year. Apple is currently testing macOS 27.1, which is scheduled for release at the end of October this year. In the medium to long term, Apple has planned a MacBook Air with M7 chips (expected in early 2027) and a brand-new MacBook Neo. Even further out (2028), an OLED MacBook Air and iMac are slated for release. Additionally, the Mac mini and Mac Studio series are testing chips such as M5 Pro, M5 Max, and M5 Ultra. These updates show Apple's continuous push for chip upgrades and screen technology innovation, though the specific timeline remains dependent on memory chip supply conditions.",
