    title_en: "Google Wallet Integrates Gmail Features, Allowing US Users to Track Online Orders and Shipping Status via the App",
    summary_en: "Google Wallet has launched a new order tracking experience for US Android users. By integrating Gmail functionality, users can now view detailed receipts, tracking numbers, and shipping status for online purchases, in addition to viewing payment credentials. When an order is nearing arrival, users can see a dedicated card below the payment carousel on the main page. Clicking this card allows users to view complete transaction information, including pricing, purchased item lists, and tracking details. This feature supports numerous US merchants, including purchases from Amazon and Google Play apps. To enable this feature, users must ensure that 'Smart features in other Google products' is enabled in their Gmail settings and re-authenticate their payment card using their Google account. Google announced that this order tracking feature is fully available to US users and supports Wear OS synchronization. This update primarily enhances the convenience of the shopping experience within the Google ecosystem and strengthens cross-service data integration capabilities.",
