    title_en: "Samsung Galaxy Z Fold 8/Ultra Improve Screen Crease: Adopting Flex Titanium for Enhanced Display Support",
    summary_en: "This article introduces Samsung's newly released Galaxy Z Fold 8 and Galaxy Z Fold 8 Ultra, noting that their most significant improvement compared to previous generations is the noticeable reduction in the inner screen crease. Historically, the crease has been a major drawback of foldable phones. Samsung claims that by incorporating a \"Flex Titanium\" display backplate for both models, replacing the original plastic components, they utilize titanium alloy film and plates to strengthen the display's support structure. This not only improves the visibility of the crease but also makes the device thinner. The author emphasizes that this improvement is particularly noticeable when viewed from non-perpendicular angles. Although long-term folding test data is lacking, Samsung expresses extreme optimism regarding the material application in the new hinge system, anticipating that the crease will not worsen with increased folding cycles. For consumers hesitant to purchase a foldable phone due to crease concerns, these two models offer a significant upgrade experience.",
