    summary_en: "This article provides an in-depth review of the newly launched Samsung Galaxy Z Fold 8 series, covering two different models with distinct designs: the Galaxy Z Fold 8 Ultra and the Galaxy Z Fold 8. The Fold 8 Ultra maintains the existing design style while upgrading to a 5,000 mAh battery, a sharper screen, and an anti-reflective coating. It also improves the hinge structure, making it easier to open and close. In contrast, the Galaxy Z Fold 8 adopts a brand-new, wider 4:3 screen ratio, offering a more compact and novel user experience. The review points out that the main upgrades on the Fold 8 Ultra are the anti-reflective coating and the more precise hinge design. However, while the 4:3 ratio of the Fold 8 brings novelty, its practicality for multitasking and web content reading is still limited due to the large amount of screen space occupied by the keyboard. These two models represent two extreme design philosophies, and users must decide based on their own balance between portability and screen utility.",
