    summary_en: "At a recent press conference, Samsung confirmed that its latest foldable phone lineup, including the Galaxy Z Fold 8, Z Fold 8 Ultra, and Z Flip 8, has adopted silicon-carbon battery technology. This battery technology significantly increases the energy density of the battery, allowing for higher capacity batteries to be packed into the same volume. Compared to the previous generation, the Z Fold 8's battery capacity increases from 4,400 mAh to 4,800 mAh, while the Z Fold 8 Ultra increases capacity to 5,000 mAh despite a thinner profile. Furthermore, Samsung has upgraded the charging specifications, providing 45W wired fast charging and 20W wireless charging for the Fold 8 and Fold 8 Ultra. Although the article notes that silicon-carbon batteries are a future trend, the increase in battery capacity in the current products is gradual. The application of this technology suggests that future foldable phones will see significant improvements in battery life and charging speed.",
