    summary_en: "This article introduces Samsung's latest models, the Galaxy Watch 9 and the Galaxy Watch Ultra 2. The Galaxy Watch 9 retains a design similar to last year's model, with key upgrades focusing on battery capacity (390mAh for the 40mm model and 445mAh for the 44mm model) and lighter straps. The flagship Galaxy Watch Ultra 2, however, adopts a more rugged design and features significant specification enhancements. The biggest highlight of the Ultra 2 is its 800mAh battery capacity, while being thinner than its predecessor, along with an impressive peak brightness of 5,000 nits, ensuring clear display in any environment. Furthermore, both watches have enhanced fitness functionalities. The Ultra 2 features an IP69K rating and EN13319 diving certification, adding functions such as diving depth and decompression guidance. Both models also incorporate a \"Raise to talk\" feature, using AI to determine if the user is checking the time or interacting with Gemini, thereby improving the user experience. Overall, Samsung continues to provide reliable wearable devices on the Wear OS platform, with the Ultra 2 particularly excelling in durability and screen performance.",
