    summary_en: "Samsung has newly launched the Galaxy Watch 9, Galaxy Watch Active 2, and Galaxy Watch Ultra 2. While the new models maintain the existing design aesthetic, their core technology has undergone a major upgrade. All new models transition from the original Exynos chipset to the Snapdragon Wear Elite, which is expected to impact daily performance and battery life. In terms of features, besides increasing the Ultra 2's battery capacity (to 800mAh) and adding support for deeper water depths (up to 40m), the new models introduce the \"Vitals\" function. This function establishes a health baseline using overnight data from heart rate, blood oxygen, and skin temperature, and also adds advanced health metrics such as \"Daily Cardio Load.\" Furthermore, the starting price for the Galaxy Watch 9 is $380 (Bluetooth version) or $430 (LTE version), representing an increase compared to the previous generation. Consumers are advised to monitor the actual performance of the chipset and utilize the advanced health tracking features for daily health management.",
