    category: "重點關注",
    title: "美國陸軍AI使用限制：AI代幣耗盡後，軍方被迫限制員工使用生成式AI工具",
    summary: "美國國防部（DOD）下屬的陸軍戰鬥能力發展司令部（DEVCOM）員工，在大量使用生成式AI工具後，收到通知必須限制AI代幣使用。此前，陸軍資訊長官（CIO）曾宣布提供無限代幣，但由於代幣池在六月中旬耗盡，軍方被迫重新設定使用限制。陸軍使用的AI平台為Ask Sage，這是一個多模態生成式AI平台，支援Gemini、Llama和ChatGPT等大型語言模型（LLMs）。該平台用於「企業級LLM工作區」，並具備處理受控未分類資訊（Controlled Unclassified Information）的認證。文章指出，陸軍員工曾被鼓勵使用生成式AI，並最初分配了每月至少20萬個代幣。代幣耗盡後，其未來是否會得到續用，目前仍不明確。",
    tags: ["美國陸軍", "生成式AI", "LLMs", "AI代幣", "DOD", "Ask Sage"],
    title_en: "US Army Limits AI Use After AI Tokens Exhaustion",
    summary_en: "Employees of the U.S. Army Combat Capabilities Development Command (DEVCOM), which falls under the Department of Defense (DOD), received notification that they must limit their use of generative AI tools after extensive usage. Previously, the Army CIO had announced the provision of unlimited tokens, but due to the token pool exhausting in mid-June, the military was forced to reset usage restrictions. The AI platform used by the Army is Ask Sage, a multimodal generative AI platform that supports large language models (LLMs) such as Gemini, Llama, and ChatGPT. This platform is used for an \"enterprise-grade LLM workspace\" and is certified to handle Controlled Unclassified Information. The article notes that Army employees were initially encouraged to use generative AI and were initially allocated at least 200,000 tokens per month. Whether this allocation will be renewed after the tokens are exhausted remains unclear.",
    tags_en: ["US Army", "Generative AI", "LLMs", "AI Tokens", "DOD", "Ask Sage"],
    sources: [
      { name: "Ars Technica", url: "https://arstechnica.com/ai/2026/07/us-army-faces-ai-use-limits-after-exhausting-years-supply-of-ai-tokens", lang: "EN" }
    ]
