    category: "重點關注",
    title: "GNOME 平台開發者分享：實現跨會話的視窗位置儲存與恢復框架",
    summary: "本文在 GUADEC 2026 大會上，由 Adrian Vovk 介紹了為 GNOME 平台開發的跨會話視窗位置儲存與恢復框架。此功能旨在解決使用者從傳統 X11 轉移到 Wayland 後，常忽略的「無法儲存和恢復視窗位置」的痛點。開發者提到，此框架經過了兩次 API 實作的失敗，但對第三次嘗試抱持信心。雖然該功能預計在 10 月份發布的 GNOME 51 版本中，但目前尚未實現，開發團隊持續努力完善此平台級的解決方案，以提升 GNOME 桌面體驗。",
    tags: ["GNOME", "Wayland", "X11", "視窗管理", "桌面環境", "GUADEC"],
    title_en: "GNOME Platform Developer Shares: A Framework for Cross-Session Window Position Saving and Restoration",
    summary_en: "At the GUADEC 2026 conference, Adrian Vovk introduced a cross-session window position saving and restoration framework developed for the GNOME platform. This feature aims to solve the often-overlooked pain point of 'inability to save and restore window positions' when users transition from traditional X11 to Wayland. The developer mentioned that the framework underwent two failed API implementations but remains confident in the third attempt. Although the feature is expected in the GNOME 51 version releasing in October, it is not yet implemented. The development team continues to work hard to perfect this platform-level solution to enhance the GNOME desktop experience.",
