    summary_en: "This article reports on OpenAI's shift in business model, as it attempts to enter the 'consulting services' domain. OpenAI has launched a service called 'Presence,' designed to help enterprises deploy AI Agents. The business logic of this model is that as foundational AI models become increasingly commoditized, OpenAI is shifting its focus to the 'plumbing' layer—that is, providing services for the deployment, integration, and implementation of AI Agents. This service requires enterprises to pay high 'on-site deployment' fees, transitioning OpenAI's business model from pure API services toward one that closely resembles traditional enterprise consulting. This signifies the AI industry moving from model competition toward a commercial phase of service and system integration, offering enterprises more concrete implementation solutions, but potentially raising the adoption barrier for small and medium-sized enterprises.",
