    title: "CIS與SAFECode發布《安全設計指引》：強化軟體開發流程，納入AI輔助安全考量",
    summary: "非營利資安組織CIS與SAFECode於7月9日發布《安全設計：軟體安全實務評估指引》1.1版。本指引以NIST安全軟體開發框架（SSDF）為基礎，涵蓋安全設計、安全開發、供應鏈安全及漏洞修補等六項核心考量。指引強調，評估重點不在於單一安全功能清單或測試結果，而是需查核安全措施是否已融入日常開發流程。開發組織應提供安全設計文件、威脅建模結果等日常產生的佐證資料。1.1版特別擴充了AI相關指引，指出AI生成的程式碼仍需遵循既有安全開發要求，必須經過安全分析工具檢查、人員審查及測試。此外，對於AI代理系統，由於其輸出具有機率性，若用於關鍵應用，建議必須由人員複核，或採用確定性邏輯的非AI軟體驗證。",
    tags: ["CIS", "SAFECode", "NIST SSDF", "安全設計", "軟體安全", "AI安全"],
    title_en: "CIS and SAFECode Release 'Secure Design Guidelines': Strengthening Software Development Processes with AI Security Considerations",
    summary_en: "The non-profit cybersecurity organization CIS and SAFECode released the 'Secure Design: Software Security Practical Assessment Guide' version 1.1 on July 9. This guide is based on the NIST Secure Software Development Framework (SSDF) and covers six core considerations: secure design, secure development, supply chain security, and vulnerability remediation. The guide emphasizes that the focus of the assessment is not on a single list of security features or test results, but rather on verifying whether security measures have been integrated into the daily development process. Development organizations should provide supporting documentation generated during daily operations, such as security design documents and threat modeling results. Version 1.1 specifically expands the AI-related guidelines, stating that AI-generated code must still adhere to existing secure development requirements and must undergo checks by security analysis tools, human review, and testing. Furthermore, for AI agent systems, due to the probabilistic nature of their output, if used in critical applications, it is recommended that the output be manually reviewed by personnel or that non-AI software with deterministic logic be used for verification.",
    tags_en: ["CIS", "SAFECode", "NIST SSDF", "Secure Design", "Software Security", "AI Security"],
